      "section": "3 · Core concept",
      "title": "What is a workshop?",
      "term": "Workshop",
      "definition": "A structured working session in which a group actively produces a concrete outcome together, rather than receiving information passively.",
      "notes": [
        "The outcome — a decision, a plan, a prototype — is agreed before the session starts",
        "If participants could be replaced by an email, it is a meeting, not a workshop"
      ],
      "source": "Demo content, fictional"
    },
